; lang.xon -- what this bundle IS.
;
; xon: read with the ordinary reader and never evaluated, like every other
; manifest in the x-lang world (pin.xon, engine.pin.xon).  A form a reader
; does not know is a loud error, never a skip.
;
; FORMAT (one form per line):
;   (lang "NAME")               the -l name
;   (dialect NAME)              he | xe | rn -- a REQUIREMENT, not a taste
;   (requires-release "TAG")    the x-lang this bundle was built against
;   (entry "FILE")              loaded AFTER the dialect, not instead of it

(lang "awk")

; RADON, determined by where this bundle is GOING rather than where it is.
; The core is deliberately pure -- program text in, output text out, which is
; what makes the suite trivial to write -- but an awk is not an awk until it
; reads files named on the command line, runs `cmd | getline`, and honours
; system(); every one of those is a Sys door, and Sys's process and file
; doors are radon opt-ins.  Declaring lighter now would mean re-declaring at
; the first getline, and a dialect row that changes per release is a row
; nobody can rely on.
(dialect rn)

; PAIRING, NOT PINNING.  This row tracks what the specs are green AGAINST.
; v0.9.0 is the release current when the bundle was scaffolded.  ONE thing
; now needs newer: the stdin slurp's 64K chunks (awk/eval.x) need the Str8
; make stack fix (x-lang 245dc6d9, post-v0.9.0) -- ride this row to the
; first release that carries it.
(requires-release "v0.9.0")

(entry "run.x")
